    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), keeping structural impact low by extracting the logic into a small, cohesive helper rather than growing any existing method.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny helper mirroring the existing `Namesakes`/`Household` pattern. `of(owner, namesakeCount)` starts at 1, adds 1 for a present email, adds 1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, and caps at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n2. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 swapped the multi-branch tier ternary for `dto.setMembershipLevel(MembershipLevel.of(owner, namesakeCount))`. This also dropped the `Household.size` dependency and lowered the method's complexity.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 computes the level once, sets it on the DTO, and records it in the create audit line (`membershipLevel={}`) \u2014 the audit line previously carried no tier, now carries the level per the spec.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string field with a `membershipLevel` integer field (min 1, max 3), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with `setMembershipLevel`/removes `membershipTier`.\n\nThe new `coreNumericLevel` test passes (unique named owner with email \u2192 `membershipLevel` 3), and the full suite is green.",
